cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite Version 0.1.0 of this research repository."
title: "New Hadamard orders above 10^4"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeffery
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/new-hadamard-orders-above-10000"
url: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/new-hadamard-orders-above-10000"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  The paper constructs Hadamard matrices of six orders: 159052 = 4·17·2339,
  824332 = 4·206083, 22425772 = 4·31·223·811, 25072 = 16·1567,
  46192 = 16·2887 and 47968 = 32·1499. The first three come from a theorem:
  a quaternary conference matrix of order n+1 with n odd and a prime
  q = 2n^r - 1 give a Hadamard matrix of order 4(2n^r + 1). The proof combines
  Turyn's power construction for conference matrices, extended to
  non-Hermitian quaternary matrices, with Kumar's 2026 quaternary form of
  Yamada's construction of order 4(q+2); the inputs are quaternary conference
  matrices of orders 142 and 322 published by Zaitsev and by Kumar. No
  construction checked by the author reaches these three orders from
  previously known ingredients. The last three come from a second
  construction, which places two dihedral Golay pairs of Kamali and
  Kharaghani on commuting tensor factors and gives a Hadamard matrix of order
  16(m+n); each is half the smallest order previously recorded for its odd
  part. The repository verifies the ingredients exactly and the large
  matrices by exact or randomized Gram checks. Novelty is bounded to the
  sources searched.
keywords:
  - Hadamard matrices
  - conference matrices
  - quaternary Hadamard matrices
  - Golay sequences
references:
  - type: article
    title: "On C-matrices of arbitrary powers"
    authors:
      - family-names: Turyn
        given-names: Richard J.
    journal: "Canadian Journal of Mathematics"
    volume: 23
    year: 1971
  - type: article
    title: "Dihedral Golay sequences"
    authors:
      - family-names: Kamali
        given-names: F.
      - family-names: Kharaghani
        given-names: Hadi
    journal: "Australasian Journal of Combinatorics"
    volume: 18
    year: 1998
  - type: software
    title: "New Hadamard matrices"
    authors:
      - family-names: Kumar
        given-names: K.
    url: "https://github.com/vatskishan03/Hadamard"
    year: 2026
